	Synchronization (Waits in selenium)
	Synchronization is the process of adjusting the speed of tool with speed of application.
	
	
	Methods to use incase of synchronization issues.
	1. Thread.sleep();
			a. pauses the entire execution for give time period.
			b. it is applicable for single statement only.
			c. Mandatory delay (it takes mandatory delay 2,3,)
	2. implicit wait (dynamic waits)
			a. It doesn't take mandatory delay (if elements loaded with 2 second then it will not wait till the time is completed.)
			b. default polling interval: 500 ms .5 seconds
			c. Only checks the existence of an element in DOM (present in DOM)
			d. Applies : driver.findElement and driver.findElements
			e. Stops early : yes, if element founds before timeout. 
			f. Exception Ignored in give time period : NOSuchElementException. 	
	3. ExplicitWait (WebDriver Wait)
			a. It doesn't take mandatory delay (if elements loaded with 2 second then it will not wait till the time is completed.)
			b. default polling interval: 500 ms .5 seconds
			c. it checks the existence along with condition (state of an element) use by tester
	4. FluentWait
			
